rcent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\\`library/video.spec.ts:699 - screencast › should capture full viewport on hidpi\\` flakes on chromium (headless-shell, e.g. bot `frozen-time-library-chromium-linux`), failing its first attempt in ~7.3% of CI runs (405/5561 in the recent test-results window), rescued by retry.\n\nFailure:\n```\nError: Expected all pixels to satisfy isAlmostRed, found bad pixel (255, 255, 255, 255)\n```\n\nThis is distinct from the previously closed issues on this test — #22411 and #22617 were both specific to headed WebKit, and the test already has `it.fixme()` guards excluding those configs. The current flake is in the headless-shell chromium config, which is not excluded and is expected to be stable.\n\nMost recently observed on PR #42191 ([run](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/actions/runs/31450894460)), unrelated to that PR's diff (which only touches trace request-duration recording).\n\nI couldn't reproduce it locally after 25 repeated runs (4 workers) on macOS, so it may be timing/load-dependent (screencast frame capture racing the pixel check) and specific to Linux CI. Filing for tracking since it wasn't previously reported for this config.","closed_by":{"login":"pavelfeldman","id":883973,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Mzk3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/883973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavelfeldman","html_url":"https://github.com/pavelfeldman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavelfeldman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavelfeldman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavelfeldman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavelfeldman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavelfeldman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavelfeldman/orgs","re